# The overlay verbs set a signal and nothing else, so a chord, a button and a
# future context menu open the same palette without three copies of the logic.

file: "packages/editor/src/gestures/commands.ts"
doc: "The one command registry every dispatcher — keymap, toolbar, context menu, palette — runs through."

constants: [
  { name: "COMMANDS"
    change_type: MODIFIED
    doc:
      "Two entries added, and one existing entry changes.\n"
      "\n"
      "ADDED 'open-palette', label 'Command Palette': sets the overlay signal\n"
      "to 'palette'. ADDED 'open-help', label 'Keyboard Shortcuts': sets it\n"
      "to 'help'. Both set unconditionally and neither toggles.\n"
      "\n"
      "MODIFIED 'escape': when ui.overlay() is not undefined, set the overlay\n"
      "to undefined and RETURN WITHOUT touching the selection. Only when no\n"
      "overlay is open does it clear the selection as it does today.\n"
      "\n"
      "Every claim above is about what these three FUNCTIONS do when invoked,\n"
      "which is how command_wiring.test.ts exercises them -- by calling\n"
      "runCommand directly, never by dispatching a key event. Which chords\n"
      "reach them end to end is a separate question owned by\n"
      "keyboard_handler, and the two do not line up everywhere: with focus in\n"
      "the palette's text input, shouldIgnoreKey returns true and NO chord\n"
      "reaches any command, so the palette is closed by its own Escape\n"
      "handler rather than by this one.\n"
      "\n"
      "The modified 'escape' therefore covers the HELP SHEET, which holds no\n"
      "text input. Ordering still matters there: closing the overlay AND\n"
      "clearing the selection on one press would discard a selection the user\n"
      "never asked to lose, and selection is not on the undo log so it could\n"
      "not be recovered. Escape twice is how a user clears a selection with\n"
      "an overlay open -- once to close, once to deselect.\n"
      "\n"
      "All three reach the overlay through context.ui, which every command\n"
      "already holds. No new CommandContext field, optional or otherwise.\n"
      "\n"
      "gestures/command_wiring.test.ts needs a change BEFORE this lands, and\n"
      "it is not only an added assertion. Its spyContext builds `ui` as a\n"
      "partial object cast `as unknown as UiState`, so the cast hides a\n"
      "missing setOverlay from the compiler while the file's\n"
      "`for (const command of COMMANDS)` loop runs every command -- the two\n"
      "new entries and the modified escape would each throw at runtime. The\n"
      "spy `ui` gains a recording overlay/setOverlay pair, and each new\n"
      "command gains its own assertion."
    type: { named: { symbol: "Array", args: [ { named: { symbol: "Command" } } ] } }
    uses: ["CommandContext", "clearSelection"]
  }
]
